| `expr is ClassName` — the type test: true exactly when `expr` is a
| particle of that class, false otherwise. Never an error — a wrong class
| or a non-particle value simply answers false, the same spirit as `=`
| being well-defined for mismatched kinds.
{
    emit Timestamp to core get t
    assert t ∈ TimestampResult
    assert not (t ∈ LengthResult)
    assert not (t._class ∈ TimestampResult)  | a string is not a particle
    assert not (1 ∈ TimestampResult)  | neither is a number
    assert not ({ x = 1 } ∈ TimestampResult)  | nor an object without _class
}
